// tdd-coverage — premise library for the execution-phase per-branch coverage
// gate (write_tests / run_final_tests).
//
// NOT model-authored: the deterministic tdd-coverage compiler
// (src/vrf/tdd-coverage-compiler.ts) generates the consuming program from a
// task's behaviors.json — the model never hand-writes this gate's facts. Each
// if/else/error branch of an invariant is one subject; the compiler feeds it an
// EXPLICIT value per phase (never UNKNOWN, so verdicts are clean CONFLICTs):
//
//   FACT tdd_cov.br_1 is_branch          // it is a branch of the task
//   FACT tdd_cov.br_1 had_red            // a test drove it and failed first
//   FACT tdd_cov.br_1 has_green          // ...and now passes
//   NOT  tdd_cov.br_2 had_red            // an uncovered branch, stated false
//   NOT  tdd_cov.br_2 has_green
//
// and binds the phase toggles via values: {"tdd_cov.red_phase": true} at
// write_tests, {"tdd_cov.suite_complete": true} at run_final_tests.
DOMAIN tdd_cov

// -- phase toggles (bound from data, one phase per gate run) --
VAR red_phase        // write_tests: every branch must have a failing test
VAR suite_complete   // run_final_tests: every branch must pass

// -- test-first discipline: a green branch was red first. A has_green with a
//    NOT had_red is a CONFLICT with a why-trace — gaming is caught in the SAT,
//    not merely in the store's status ladder. --
PREMISE no_green_without_red FOR EACH b MENTIONED:
    WHEN b has_green
    THEN b had_red

// -- the red-phase gate: claiming the red phase demands every branch has a
//    failing test; an uncovered branch is NAMED as a CONFLICT. --
PREMISE red_phase_needs_all_red FOR EACH b MENTIONED:
    WHEN red_phase
    AND  b is_branch
    THEN b had_red

// -- the green-phase gate: claiming the suite complete demands every branch
//    passes; an unpassed branch is NAMED. --
PREMISE complete_needs_all_green FOR EACH b MENTIONED:
    WHEN suite_complete
    AND  b is_branch
    THEN b has_green
